          }
        ],
        "SafeERC20FailedOperation(address)": [
          {
            "details": "An operation with an ERC-20 token failed."
          }
        ]
      },
      "kind": "dev",
      "methods": {
        "executeBuyFist()": {
          "details": "Price policy: \"how much FIST is 1 OSK worth\" (rFist/rOsk). Requirement L63 text: \"buy 5% when the price drops 10% ... a single buy is worth at most 1000 usd,   if one buy does not meet the target then buy in multiple batches, and once met stop supporting the market that day\" --   so the buy side is a **batched** mechanism: a single buy <= 1000 USD value, and if the target is not met it can be called again the same day;   once the price returns to the -5% target, todayBuyFistFinished is set and no more buying happens that day. Pitfall (severe): `todayBuyFistFinished` must be **reset on a new day** (handled by `_resetBuyFistDay()`) --   if it is only set true and never reset, then after the first target is met the flag stays true forever and the buy side is permanently crippled. Pitfall: the new-day check must come **before** the `todayBuyFistFinished` guard, otherwise the reset can never happen. Pitfall: CEI -- record the day's cumulative amount first, then perform the external swap interaction."
        },
        "executeSellFist()": {
          "details": "Target: push back down to ref + 3% (SELL_TARGET_RISE_BP). Pitfall: once per cycle -- a second call in the same cycle reverts (cycle = PERIOD_SECONDS: production 1 day / FAST_TEST 1 hour)."
        },
        "owner()": {
          "details": "Returns the address of the current owner."
        },
        "renounceOwnership()": {
          "details": "Leaves the contract without owner. It will not be possible to call `onlyOwner` functions. Can only be called by the current owner. NOTE: Renouncing ownership will leave the contract without an owner, thereby disabling any functionality that is only available to the owner."
        },
        "setMaxRefDeviationBp(uint256)": {
          "details": "0 disables clamping (not recommended). The upper bound is BP (10000) = 100%."
        },
        "transferOwnership(address)": {
          "details": "Transfers ownership of the contract to a new account (`newOwner`). Can only be called by the current owner."
        }
      },
      "stateVariables": {
        "PERIOD_SECONDS": {
          "details": "Market-making cycle length (seconds) -- the cycle basis for reference price locking and \"sell once a day\".      Production = **1 day**; when `GlobalConfig.FAST_TEST = true` it shortens to **1 hour**,      so that \"support the market successfully once a day\" can be reproduced within 1 hour in fast tests.      Evidence: the client requested on 2026-09-26 \"change the insurance pool's once-a-day successful market support to once an hour\". Pitfall: unrelated to `Treasury.REFILL_COOLDOWN` -- the latter is the treasury refill cooldown, and the two are independent."
        },
        "maxRefDeviationBp": {
          "details": "The reference price snapshot's **single-period maximum deviation** (bp). Prevents manipulating the spot reserves at a cycle boundary to lock in a distorted reference price.      Default 2000 (20%). Setting it to 0 disables clamping (not recommended)."
        }
      },
      "version": 1
    },
    "userdoc": {
      "kind": "user",
      "methods": {
        "executeBuyFist()": {
          "notice": "FIST market support buy: when OSK depreciates >=10% against FIST, use the FIST reserve to buy OSK"
        },
        "executeSellFist()": {
          "notice": "FIST market support sell: when OSK appreciates >=10% against FIST, sell OSK back for FIST"
        },
        "setBToken(address)": {
          "notice": "Set the FIST token address (market-making payment token)"
        },
        "setMaxRefDeviationBp(uint256)": {
          "notice": "Set the FIST reference price's single-period maximum deviation (bp)"
        },
        "setOskFistPair(address)": {
          "notice": "Set the OSK/FIST pair (market support target)"
        },
        "updateDailyReferenceFist()": {
          "notice": "Refresh the FIST channel's intraday reference price (public keeper entry point)"
        }
      },
      "version": 1
    }
  },
